From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 08:51:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: pmdomain: Store cached power-down state index
 as an unsigned int

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

genpd caches the state index selected by the governor so the next
power-down decision can reuse it while constraints remain unchanged.

The cache currently stores the index in a bool, truncating every index
above 1. Use unsigned int to match generic_pm_domain.state_idx and preserve
the complete selected index. Domains that only select state 0 or 1 are
unchanged.

Fixes: e94999688e3a ("PM / Domains: Add genpd governor for CPUs")
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Reviewed-by: Ishan Shah <ishah@nvidia.com>
Assisted-by: OpenAI-Codex:gpt-5.6
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit d47f864c8037577cc2a8754a6263a676d9028417 resolute:linux-nvidia-bos)
Signed-off-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00620
Ledger-Origin: nvidia@66b06fb76d4de81bd76764c366415f2e37de27e4
---
 include/linux/pm_domain.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/pm_domain.h b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
index f925614aebdb..103e74486eba 100644
--- a/include/linux/pm_domain.h
+++ b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
@@ -171,7 +171,7 @@ struct genpd_governor_data {
 	ktime_t last_enter;
 	bool reflect_residency;
 	bool cached_power_down_ok;
-	bool cached_power_down_state_idx;
+	unsigned int cached_power_down_state_idx;
 };
 
 struct genpd_power_state {
